WEBVTT

00:09.030 --> 00:14.360
Thanks for bringing me that message from 
Cecilia even on your day off, Teal.

00:14.370 --> 00:16.030
Oh, don't worry about me.

00:16.030 --> 00:19.330
I wanted to visit the guardian 
deity, and it was on my way.

00:19.330 --> 00:20.730
I... see.

00:21.050 --> 00:24.040
Anyway, I'm gonna go. Get some rest.

00:24.040 --> 00:25.620
Take care out there.

00:27.500 --> 00:30.520
Teal was acting awfully docile.

00:31.090 --> 00:33.860
Oh, my guardian deity!

00:33.860 --> 00:37.010
I stayed respectful of the time and place

00:37.010 --> 00:39.500
and controlled myself, just like you said!

00:39.500 --> 00:42.350
Don't get all excited! 
You'll collapse again!

00:42.350 --> 00:46.810
Look! I have some of the 
magicite you love so much!

00:46.810 --> 00:48.960
You found such fine ore for me?

00:48.960 --> 00:51.430
I'll work my very hardest,

00:51.430 --> 00:54.340
so please eat all you like! 
Don't hold back!

00:54.340 --> 00:57.950
I'd like you to think carefully 
about what you just said.

01:03.140 --> 01:05.990
So Gar's basically just a 
gigolo at this point, huh?

01:05.990 --> 01:08.160
You mustn't laugh.

01:08.160 --> 01:12.780
But it's clear how much Teal 
genuinely loves Gar, isn't it?

01:16.130 --> 01:17.380
Yoki?

01:17.380 --> 01:20.640
Oh... This tea's really good.

01:20.640 --> 01:23.640
Maybe all my practice 
is starting to pay off.

01:29.970 --> 01:32.790
Today was fun, as always...

01:33.230 --> 01:36.680
but do I really want 
things to stay this way?

03:10.590 --> 03:11.460
And...

03:11.460 --> 03:13.960
why did you call me over for this?

03:14.200 --> 03:17.780
There's no one else I can 
turn to for love advice!

03:17.780 --> 03:18.840
Please!

03:18.840 --> 03:22.450
Well, Captain... you have 
no friends, after all.

03:22.450 --> 03:25.760
Rude! I have friends!

03:25.760 --> 03:28.990
And? What did you do this time?

03:29.300 --> 03:31.940
I told you, I just want some love advice!

03:31.940 --> 03:37.080
Look, you know how I can use Vanish 
Wave to turn invisible, right?

03:38.090 --> 03:40.070
So after saying goodbye to Cecilia,

03:40.070 --> 03:44.580
I was wondering what she 
might be doing, so...

03:52.540 --> 03:54.430
Not good enough!

03:54.430 --> 03:55.790
I'm not done yet!

03:55.790 --> 04:00.800
I had no idea Cecilia was 
putting in that much effort.

04:00.800 --> 04:04.050
And that made me worry that maybe

04:04.050 --> 04:07.220
I really don't know the girl 
I love that well at all.

04:07.770 --> 04:09.310
That's incredibly creepy.

04:09.700 --> 04:10.430
Huh?

04:10.430 --> 04:14.860
Can I arrest you for unlawful 
entry and stalking?

04:14.860 --> 04:18.260
I just came here for some love advice!

04:18.260 --> 04:19.420
I swear...

04:20.020 --> 04:22.950
Well, I don't think things 
are going too badly.

04:23.580 --> 04:26.960
But for all your hollering 
that you love Cecilia so much,

04:26.960 --> 04:28.530
you're not aggressive enough!

04:28.930 --> 04:31.500
From my perspective, you're a coward!

04:31.500 --> 04:32.540
Wha?!

04:32.910 --> 04:37.780
Do you just want to be her 
teatime companion forever?

04:37.780 --> 04:39.550
W-Well...

04:39.770 --> 04:44.300
You can't make any progress if you 
barely know anything about her.

04:44.860 --> 04:46.090
That's true...

04:47.400 --> 04:48.750
Thanks, Duke.

04:48.750 --> 04:50.120
Just one thing:

04:50.810 --> 04:53.080
don't be a stalker.

04:53.080 --> 04:53.820
Right.

04:54.290 --> 04:55.640
A stalker?

04:57.230 --> 05:00.820
So... are you actually a 
criminal, not an ordinary civilian?

05:00.820 --> 05:03.060
Er, no, it's not like that...

05:03.420 --> 05:06.070
You showed up at just the right time.

05:06.820 --> 05:10.860
I'm leaving the rest to someone 
who knows Cecilia well.

05:10.860 --> 05:11.730
Huh?!

05:15.020 --> 05:16.820
S-So...

05:17.130 --> 05:20.470
Please tell me everything 
you know about Cecilia.

05:20.470 --> 05:23.080
Gross. Zero points.

05:21.610 --> 05:23.970
DUKE ASKED ME TO COME.

05:23.970 --> 05:26.840
Also, would you just use your voice?

05:27.210 --> 05:29.390
You were talking last time.

05:30.100 --> 05:32.780
"No. That was a special exception."

05:30.240 --> 05:35.350
NO. THAT WAS A SPECIAL EXCEPTION.

05:32.780 --> 05:35.350
Jeez, I'm sorry, okay?!

05:37.170 --> 05:40.660
Okay, I guess I can't make you 
talk if you don't want to.

05:41.380 --> 05:43.870
Anyway, you want to know about Cecilia?

05:44.420 --> 05:47.860
I do owe you for the advice 
you gave me before,

05:47.860 --> 05:49.490
so I'll tell you.

05:49.870 --> 05:50.960
Please do!

05:50.960 --> 05:52.990
Okay, let's see...

05:53.410 --> 05:58.500
I don't think the hero's party 
would exist without Cecilia.

05:58.500 --> 06:00.850
Did you guys get hurt that often?

06:00.850 --> 06:03.500
That's not what I mean. But first...

06:03.500 --> 06:06.610
there's the problem of all 
the women who flock to Yuga.

06:07.250 --> 06:08.310
Hi!

06:09.470 --> 06:15.350
CHILL OUT.

06:09.470 --> 06:12.210
The swordsman's written 
notes didn't stop them,

06:10.990 --> 06:15.350
Cut it out already!

06:12.210 --> 06:15.350
and when I stepped in, things 
just got more heated.

06:16.070 --> 06:17.090
Move it!

06:17.090 --> 06:18.480
Out of our way!

06:18.480 --> 06:21.620
Everyone, please calm down.

06:22.060 --> 06:26.110
But Cecilia always calmed 
the storm for us.

06:27.240 --> 06:30.950
"She did almost all of 
the background work."

06:31.320 --> 06:33.060
Uh, you should all be sharing that.

06:33.060 --> 06:35.740
W-We do things when we can!

06:35.310 --> 06:48.010
WE DIVIDED UP THE TASKS WE COULD DIVIDE UP.
I WAS THE COOK.

06:35.740 --> 06:39.080
"We divided up the tasks 
we could divide up.

06:39.080 --> 06:42.210
I was the cook." Really?

06:42.210 --> 06:45.990
Well, you know I can't cook!

06:46.420 --> 06:48.010
And what about Yuga?

06:48.010 --> 06:51.480
He can, but whenever he goes 
out to gather ingredients,

06:51.480 --> 06:53.760
he always finds trouble to get into.

06:56.390 --> 06:59.950
Cecilia and I were in 
charge of gathering intel.

07:00.460 --> 07:02.770
Since our swordsman's so useless, y'know.

07:03.020 --> 07:05.610
Cecilia managed our money, too.

07:06.010 --> 07:08.780
So Yuga contributed nothing at all?!

07:11.470 --> 07:14.570
Maybe not, but the incidents he caused

07:14.970 --> 07:18.020
always ended up helping someone somehow.

07:18.930 --> 07:21.970
I'm glad Yuga was our hero.

07:21.970 --> 07:24.030
His kindness is the real deal.

07:27.010 --> 07:31.180
I see. I feel like I understand 
Yuga a little better now.

07:31.930 --> 07:35.720
But that's not what I want! 
I was asking about Cecilia!

07:38.670 --> 07:40.950
Was there anything else?

07:42.090 --> 07:44.610
Oh, right. She had that nickname.

07:44.610 --> 07:45.830
What nickname?

07:45.830 --> 07:48.600
You don't know? Oh, it was brilliant!

07:48.600 --> 07:49.820
Cecilia was...

07:49.820 --> 07:52.820
You seem to be having a fun conversation.

07:53.870 --> 07:54.820
Cecilia?!

07:55.060 --> 07:56.850
What are you doing here?

07:57.320 --> 08:00.700
I was looking for you, Mikana. 
I wanted to talk to you.

08:00.700 --> 08:03.710
We were just... talking 
about old memories...

08:04.020 --> 08:07.970
I want to talk about old 
memories with you, too.

08:07.970 --> 08:10.710
At length, I assure you.

08:11.080 --> 08:13.340
Yoki, Raven,

08:13.630 --> 08:16.350
we'll be taking our leave for today.

08:16.350 --> 08:17.450
What?!

08:17.850 --> 08:21.400
Why only me?!

08:22.910 --> 08:28.970
Yoki, I'm sorry, but it's not my 
place to tell you Cecilia's nickname.

08:28.970 --> 08:30.130
I-It's okay.

08:30.730 --> 08:34.750
Mikana's noble sacrifice taught 
me one of Cecilia's landmines.

08:35.180 --> 08:37.640
Yoki, do you still have some time?

08:43.250 --> 08:46.930
This is the orphanage where Cecilia 
does a lot of volunteer work.

08:46.930 --> 08:48.380
Huh...

08:48.380 --> 08:51.340
Oh! It's the Cold-blooded Swordsman!

08:51.990 --> 08:54.050
Cold-blooded Swordsman!

08:54.050 --> 08:55.820
Cold-blooded Swordsman?

08:55.450 --> 08:58.050
THAT'S MY NICKNAME.

08:56.500 --> 08:58.050
Ah.

08:58.050 --> 09:00.300
Cold-blooded Swordsman!

09:00.300 --> 09:02.520
He has no blood or tears!

09:02.940 --> 09:05.560
You guys don't even know 
what that expression means.

09:05.560 --> 09:07.860
Hey, where's the Holy Mother?

09:07.860 --> 09:09.060
Holy Mother?

09:09.060 --> 09:11.470
Isn't the Holy Mother coming today?

09:11.470 --> 09:14.070
I wanna eat the Holy Mother's desserts!

09:16.070 --> 09:19.580
Thank you, Cold-blooded Swordsman!

09:20.910 --> 09:23.850
Since I don't speak when I fight,

09:23.850 --> 09:28.790
people seem to see me as a cold-blooded 
man who sheds no blood or tears.

09:29.460 --> 09:31.990
So that's why you're the 
Cold-blooded Swordsman.

09:32.420 --> 09:35.660
Yuga's nickname is "the Wandering Hero."

09:36.140 --> 09:39.890
Mikana's is "the Guardian," 
or "the Eternal Friend."

09:39.890 --> 09:42.030
I'm kinda curious
where those came from...

09:42.030 --> 09:44.350
But Cecilia...

09:44.940 --> 09:48.170
Why doesn't she like being 
called the Holy Mother?

09:49.090 --> 09:50.710
It's not my place to tell you.

09:51.070 --> 09:53.820
But you can just learn 
more about it from now on.

09:54.200 --> 09:56.310
I'm sure you'll have opportunities.

09:56.310 --> 09:57.740
I guess so.

09:58.320 --> 10:02.210
But if you don't know what 
to do once you find out...

10:05.320 --> 10:09.210
Never mind. Anyway, what 
are you going to do now?

10:09.690 --> 10:11.870
Yeah, that's the question, huh?

10:11.870 --> 10:16.830
It'd be best if I could get to know 
Cecilia better and get closer to her...

10:17.330 --> 10:19.810
Why don't you take on a quest with her?

10:19.810 --> 10:23.130
I mean... thanks to you, I...

10:23.510 --> 10:24.350
That's it!

10:25.820 --> 10:30.070
When the heroine is in a tight spot, 
the protagonist gallantly saves her!

10:30.070 --> 10:32.610
And from there, love is inevitably born!

10:35.050 --> 10:39.470
"Operation I'm a Protagonist, 
Too" begins now!

10:43.190 --> 10:46.460
I managed to get Cecilia to agree.

10:47.090 --> 10:49.390
Today's the day I show her what I can do!

10:49.390 --> 10:50.370
And then...

10:50.890 --> 10:52.360
Good morning.

10:56.340 --> 10:58.150
Why are you here?

10:58.150 --> 11:00.890
The swordsman asked me to accompany you.

11:00.890 --> 11:03.250
Something else came up, apparently.

11:03.560 --> 11:05.340
Raven!

11:05.340 --> 11:07.220
So what are we doing?

11:07.220 --> 11:09.730
You want to show Cecilia 
what you can do, right?

11:09.730 --> 11:11.730
I do have a plan.

11:11.730 --> 11:15.230
Let's hear it. I'll score it for you.

11:15.230 --> 11:16.440
Score it?

11:16.850 --> 11:21.240
The quest is to get rid of some undead 
that have made their den in a mansion.

11:21.640 --> 11:24.240
That'll be a great chance 
for Cecilia to shine.

11:24.240 --> 11:24.970
Huh?

11:25.290 --> 11:26.570
Uh, won't it?

11:26.570 --> 11:27.820
Well, I was thinking...

11:30.000 --> 11:32.020
Just leave this to me!

11:33.020 --> 11:35.500
Yoki, you're the best!

11:35.500 --> 11:39.510
So... my dream was that I'd mow 
down all the undead myself...

11:40.730 --> 11:42.260
Thirty points.

11:42.260 --> 11:43.340
Harsh!

11:44.280 --> 11:47.570
Are you dumb?! Cecilia is a priestess!

11:47.570 --> 11:50.270
Dealing with undead is her specialty!

11:50.270 --> 11:51.270
Oh.

11:51.270 --> 11:54.260
Your problem is that you base 
all your plans around yourself!

11:54.260 --> 11:57.720
Your priority should be 
what Cecilia will think!

11:57.720 --> 11:59.780
I-I'm sorry...

12:01.570 --> 12:05.710
Well, you and Cecilia can 
be the main fighters today.

12:05.710 --> 12:08.030
I'll be on support.

12:08.030 --> 12:10.730
You two need to work together 
to defeat the enemy.

12:11.180 --> 12:14.030
You want to form a relationship 
of trust, don't you?

12:14.030 --> 12:17.050
I-I get it. I think I can do that.

12:17.050 --> 12:18.550
Sorry to keep you waiting.

12:18.870 --> 12:20.670
Huh? Mikana?

12:20.670 --> 12:23.030
I'll be tagging along on this quest.

12:23.030 --> 12:25.260
Oh, that's very reassuring!

12:25.260 --> 12:28.180
Actually, I brought someone else, too.

12:28.180 --> 12:29.650
Happiness!

12:30.350 --> 12:31.180
Hi.

12:31.510 --> 12:33.220
Thanks for your help the other day.

12:33.220 --> 12:34.020
Thanks.

12:34.920 --> 12:37.690
Okay, shall we get going?

12:41.940 --> 12:43.230
This is it.

12:43.700 --> 12:46.890
All right! Let's take out those undead!

12:46.890 --> 12:47.910
Yay.

12:48.250 --> 12:49.740
Hold it right there!

12:49.740 --> 12:51.610
Did you forget the plan already?

12:51.610 --> 12:52.910
Oh, yeah!

12:53.150 --> 12:56.330
So anyway, Cecilia and I 
will take the front line.

12:56.330 --> 12:59.420
Mikana and Happiness, you're 
the rear guard. Okay?

13:05.220 --> 13:08.390
She's not giving the slightest 
hint of being afraid of ghosts.

13:09.560 --> 13:11.350
I guess that's to be expected.

13:16.650 --> 13:18.740
And there they are already.

13:18.740 --> 13:20.070
Holy Circle!

13:27.310 --> 13:29.460
Wow, that was quick.

13:29.460 --> 13:30.530
That's Cecilia for you.

13:34.040 --> 13:35.470
I'll take these.

13:41.910 --> 13:43.310
Holy Circle!

13:50.430 --> 13:52.430
Are you tired, Cecilia?

13:52.430 --> 13:54.070
I'm just fine.

13:54.070 --> 13:57.260
Holy Circle is an essential 
spell for any priest.

13:57.260 --> 13:59.580
I've boosted my magic efficiency for it.

13:59.580 --> 14:00.710
Okay.

14:00.710 --> 14:04.030
I think it's still a good idea 
to stay hydrated, though.

14:04.610 --> 14:05.990
Thank you.

14:05.990 --> 14:07.740
Well, that was thoughtful.

14:08.120 --> 14:10.960
Our captain is like that.

14:10.960 --> 14:14.120
Yeah, I guess he's the type to 
take off in weird directions

14:14.120 --> 14:15.860
when he overthinks things.

14:18.950 --> 14:20.990
This is the last room.

14:21.860 --> 14:25.180
You never see this many undead 
packed into such a small space.

14:25.180 --> 14:27.380
It's clear they have a leader.

14:27.950 --> 14:28.900
In other words...

14:28.900 --> 14:31.510
This is where we'll find the boss.

14:40.920 --> 14:41.900
That's...

14:41.900 --> 14:43.800
an Undead King.

14:43.800 --> 14:48.360
Sure looks important with 
that crown on its head.

14:49.190 --> 14:50.410
Are they strong?

14:50.410 --> 14:55.420
An Undead King's strength isn't much 
different from that of normal undead.

14:55.860 --> 14:58.430
They just have a bit more intelligence.

14:58.830 --> 14:59.920
Wimp.

14:59.920 --> 15:03.080
It doesn't live up to 
its name at all, then.

15:04.440 --> 15:07.810
Now, dead one who has taken up 
residence in someone else's house

15:07.810 --> 15:09.620
without consent!

15:09.620 --> 15:12.420
We will return you to the afterlife!

15:12.420 --> 15:13.430
Pathetic.

15:14.630 --> 15:16.890
Just who are you people?

15:17.490 --> 15:20.220
Hey! We have intruders!

15:20.220 --> 15:22.410
Your buddies won't be coming.

15:22.410 --> 15:23.400
What?!

15:23.910 --> 15:27.860
The only undead left in here is you!

15:43.120 --> 15:47.630
And now you're just an ordinary skeleton!

15:53.130 --> 15:53.960
Huh?

15:59.020 --> 16:00.450
Yoki...

16:00.450 --> 16:02.000
You are...

16:02.000 --> 16:03.140
...scum.

16:03.140 --> 16:06.680
Wait, uh... It was just a little prank...

16:07.520 --> 16:08.720
Fiend.

16:08.720 --> 16:09.570
Again, I didn't—

16:09.570 --> 16:10.780
Brute.

16:10.780 --> 16:12.920
Give me a chance to explain myself!

16:13.620 --> 16:16.830
How dare you... How dare you...

16:16.830 --> 16:21.750
How dare you?! How dare you?! 
How dare you?! How dare you?!

16:22.050 --> 16:23.780
I'm sorry, okay?!

16:26.500 --> 16:27.990
In that case...

16:29.350 --> 16:30.510
How about this one?!

16:39.500 --> 16:40.890
I lose.

16:41.340 --> 16:43.510
How very honorable of you.

16:43.510 --> 16:45.400
You won't resist anymore?

16:46.530 --> 16:48.400
I've lost.

16:51.050 --> 16:53.900
I have lost.

16:53.900 --> 16:57.800
Cecilia, it sounds like 
he's resigned himself.

16:58.380 --> 17:00.900
Use Holy Circle to put 
a quick end to this.

17:06.650 --> 17:09.380
Why are you so attached to that crown?

17:09.380 --> 17:12.530
This crown was important to me.

17:12.840 --> 17:14.870
I don't know why.

17:14.870 --> 17:17.390
It was just very important.

17:17.390 --> 17:19.970
It was important to you?

17:20.910 --> 17:24.890
Maybe you were the king of some 
nation when you were alive.

17:26.680 --> 17:27.740
All right.

17:29.900 --> 17:33.400
I'll send you to the afterlife 
along with your crown.

17:35.900 --> 17:37.530
The way she's handling this...

17:50.440 --> 17:51.820
Heaven's Rondo.

17:57.090 --> 17:59.460
I feel so nostalgic...

18:00.270 --> 18:02.180
I hear a voice.

18:02.500 --> 18:04.490
The voice of...

18:07.270 --> 18:11.400
Cecilia! You shouldn't 
use such advanced magic!

18:11.400 --> 18:14.930
Well, we've gotten rid of all the undead.

18:14.930 --> 18:16.390
That's mission complete.

18:17.210 --> 18:20.150
True. Shall we go home, then?

18:20.150 --> 18:23.220
But Mikana and Happiness, since 
you didn't do any work here,

18:23.220 --> 18:26.070
why don't you go check around the mansion?

18:26.890 --> 18:28.670
Oh, fine!

18:28.670 --> 18:29.780
We'll work.

18:30.110 --> 18:33.300
We'll meet back at the carriage.

18:33.300 --> 18:36.360
So, Cecilia, can I lend you my shoulder?

18:36.680 --> 18:38.300
Or carry you on my back?

18:40.420 --> 18:41.800
I'm sorry...

18:43.480 --> 18:45.170
I'll take that shoulder.

18:46.890 --> 18:49.020
You used too much magic, huh?

18:50.910 --> 18:54.780
I wasn't sure if he'd be able 
to take his crown with him.

18:55.450 --> 18:57.820
He sure looked happy, though.

19:01.310 --> 19:03.240
Looks like she can't make it.

19:04.590 --> 19:05.740
Yoki?!

19:06.090 --> 19:09.210
Th-This is embarrassing...

19:09.210 --> 19:11.290
Don't worry.

19:11.290 --> 19:15.170
I'll move as fast as I can so 
the other two don't see us.

19:24.850 --> 19:26.360
Why...

19:26.850 --> 19:28.830
are you guys so far apart?

19:29.460 --> 19:30.660
Trouble?

19:35.990 --> 19:38.360
Well, this is our stop.

19:38.360 --> 19:40.950
Okay. Good work today.

19:41.430 --> 19:42.360
Bye.

19:43.810 --> 19:46.370
Well? What's my score?

19:46.370 --> 19:48.870
Oh, you remembered, huh?

19:49.770 --> 19:51.250
Just tell me.

19:54.750 --> 19:55.830
No score.

19:55.830 --> 19:56.750
Huh?

19:56.750 --> 20:00.260
Sorry, but I'm not going 
to score that one.

20:00.610 --> 20:04.000
Huh?! You mean it wasn't even scorable?!

20:04.000 --> 20:05.970
No, it's not that.

20:05.970 --> 20:08.010
But that's for the best.

20:11.150 --> 20:15.290
Don't overthink everything. Just 
do the best at what you can do.

20:15.290 --> 20:17.220
That sounds kinda noncommittal.

20:17.220 --> 20:21.360
Not at all. It's the 
best advice I can give.

20:23.360 --> 20:25.270
Well, I'm going home.

20:25.270 --> 20:27.370
Okay. Thanks for today.

20:30.330 --> 20:33.820
I'll have to work hard, too.

20:38.150 --> 20:39.300
By the way,

20:39.300 --> 20:42.590
I heard you visited the orphanage.

20:43.620 --> 20:45.790
The kids told me.

20:48.550 --> 20:52.390
If you found out my nickname, 
I have to ask you...

20:52.390 --> 20:55.060
Please don't ever call me that.

20:55.060 --> 20:59.280
Oh, sure. I won't do 
anything you don't like.

20:59.280 --> 21:02.070
But... can I ask why?

21:03.080 --> 21:04.570
Well...

21:04.890 --> 21:07.060
Of course, if you don't 
want to, that's fine.

21:07.060 --> 21:10.090
It's just... it really suits you, I think.

21:11.690 --> 21:16.840
The way you spoke to the Undead King... 
You just had this air of sanctity.

21:17.770 --> 21:20.210
It reminded me of that time 
in the Demon King's castle.

21:20.210 --> 21:22.960
Back then, you really 
reminded me of a saint.

21:23.470 --> 21:27.470
Yeah. I felt like a saint 
was reaching out to me.

21:27.970 --> 21:30.430
A... saint?

21:32.430 --> 21:34.130
I mean... er...

21:39.080 --> 21:40.300
All right.

21:42.980 --> 21:45.980
I'll tell you why they 
call me Holy Mother.

21:45.980 --> 21:49.720
It's a famous story, so it's better than 
letting you hear it from someone else.

21:51.100 --> 21:53.240
You're so amazing, Cecilia!

21:53.240 --> 21:55.170
You're good at cooking and sewing,

21:55.170 --> 21:58.070
and at gathering intel and 
handling our money, too!

21:58.070 --> 21:59.630
You're...

21:59.630 --> 22:01.380
just like a mom!

22:04.850 --> 22:11.320
From then on, he started calling me 
"Mom" in front of people all the time.

22:12.140 --> 22:14.090
Stop laughing!

22:16.140 --> 22:20.130
For crying out loud! I couldn't 
have a child as big as him!

22:20.130 --> 22:20.980
Sorry...

22:21.460 --> 22:23.450
Come on, Yoki!
